Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm850-lenovo-yoga-c630: enable two-lane DP

Enable the external DisplayPort controller on the right-hand USB-C port,
register the combo PHY as a Type-C mode switch, and describe the two DP
lanes used by this board. Without the lane limit the driver defaults to
four lanes and link training fails with the tested USB-C HDMI cable.

The two-lane setting follows the earlier Yoga C630 DisplayPort proposal:
https://lkml.iu.edu/2208.1/02295.html

Display output was tested at 3840x2160 at 30 Hz and 2560x1440 near 60 Hz.
Direct VMM7100 cable unplug still causes display timeouts and an external
abort in the DP diagnostic snapshot path; this patch does not fix that.
An Anker HDMI dock survives USB-C disconnect/reconnect at the same video
link settings. See README.md for observations and remaining investigation.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm850-lenovo-yoga-c630.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm850-lenovo-yoga-c630.dts
@@ -596,6 +596,14 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&mdss_dp {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&mdss_dp_out {
+	data-lanes = <0 1>;
+};
+
 &mdss_dsi0 {
 	status = "okay";
 	vdda-supply = <&vreg_l26a_1p2>;
@@ -861,6 +869,7 @@
 
 &usb_1_qmpphy {
 	status = "okay";
+	mode-switch;
 
 	vdda-phy-supply = <&vdda_usb1_ss_core>;
 	vdda-pll-supply = <&vdda_usb1_ss_1p2>;
